      "message": "Hi Zhengping, AFAIU, We have 2 options to solve the current situation \n\nOption 1: Merge all the required dependent CL\u0027s from Open source bluetooth-next kernel (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/bluetooth/bluetooth-next.git/commit/?id\u003d69050f8d6d075dc01af7a5f2f550a8067510366f) and follow the DDK process as you suggested \n\nOption 2: Only the current CL could be updated only for Android by keeping \"removal \u003d kzalloc(*removal, GFP_ATOMIC);\" instead of moving to the latest kernel API changes \"removal \u003d kzalloc_obj(*removal, GFP_ATOMIC);\". Please note that only the current CL would be Android specific. \n\nPlease suggest your feedback on the above approches.",
